  "change": "Captured public bytes arrive over root stdin and become root-owned read-only files in private container tmpfs; no transient host staging bind. Same network/rootfs/capability limits and unprivileged subject identity; no retries.",
  "observation": "Earlier full suites exposed intermittent Docker Desktop pre-start mount failures. The small 80-bind/80-tmpfs diagnostic passed both and did not identify Docker internals as a root cause.",
  "scope": "Executed family-boundary control coverage, not exhaustive Cartesian route coverage, real-model qualification, or a universal Docker reliability guarantee. Full selected populations are separately exercised by the complete maintained suite.",
  "units": [
    {
      "name": "protected transport without per-cell host mounts captures exact public bytes on stdin, not argv or a host bind, and keeps isolation",
      "status": "passed"
    },
    {
      "name": "protected transport without per-cell host mounts retains bounded Docker startup diagnostics and labels setup, not a subject artifact",
      "status": "passed"
    },
    {
      "name": "protected transport without per-cell host mounts keeps missing submission files distinct from startup errors",
      "status": "passed"
    },
    {
      "name": "protected transport without per-cell host mounts labels malformed host JSON as protocol, not a bad submission",
      "status": "passed"
    },
    {
      "name": "protected transport without per-cell host mounts retains wall-clock exhaustion as an execution error without retrying",
